/E (I am extremely proud that I was able to even finish this project, even if I was just able to tackle one. The dataset I have chosen actually made the synthetic data generation part very difficult on our end, given that the dataset has lots of tables, lots of hidden assumptions, and some anomalies. I am also proud that we were able to create an algorithm that works pretty well. Not only does it have user freedom, where the user can have a lot of control over the parameters and distributions, but it also has tons of validity checks to ensure that the resulting dataset mimics real-life scenarios.)
